-- title:
--   Stalk dimensions on X_O: ≤ 2 on the closed fibre, 1 at component generic points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$ and $M\neq 0$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ for $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb L` of the function field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb Q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), and write $X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the morphism glued out of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_\nu:C_\nu\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ ($\nu=1,2$) be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral and integral, equipped with closed immersions $i_\nu$ over $k$ into the base change $X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}k$; assume every point of $X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that the fibre product of $i_1$ and $i_2$ is reduced with cardinality $n>0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain, with a ring map $\rho_O:A\to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, a map $\mathrm{to}\kappa:O\to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ the structure map $A\to k$, and a morphism $bc:X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}k\to X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}O$ commuting with the first projections and with the second projections up to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Then every point $y$ of $X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}O$ lying over the closed point of $O$ has $\operatorname{ringKrullDim}$ of its stalk at most $2$, and the stalks at the images under $i_\nu$ followed by $bc$ of the generic points of $C_1$ and $C_2$ both have $\operatorname{ringKrullDim}$ equal to $1$.
--
--   This is the local dimension bookkeeping for the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ after unramified base change from $A$ to $O$: the closed fibre is a curve, so stalks over the closed point of $O$ have dimension at most $2$, while the images of the generic points of the two special-fibre components $C_1,C_2$ are codimension-one points of $X\times_A\operatorname{Spec}O$. It feeds the invertibility statement for the ideal sheaf cut out by the two components after base change.
